From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Playport authors <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 23:50:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] FEXCore: reset the call-return stack with one decommit on iOS

ResetCallRetStack runs, under the code invalidation mutex, for every
thread with blocks in a range a code invalidation clears. Its
VirtualDontNeed was three Wine calls: a VirtualQuery for the protection,
a MEM_DECOMMIT and a MEM_COMMIT. In World of Warcraft's x64 client the
resets cost 57 us on average over the last owner play, 129 us over the
one before, and 175 us in its self-modifying-code bursts (16,384 resets,
2.86 s of the 13 s from 23:00:12 in the 2026-11-01 owner session),
against 16 us in a quiet process. They are almost all of the 190 us each
access-violation invalidation took ([inv-census] av), and the 16-minute
play spent 75 s in them.

On iOS Wine's decommit (virtual_ios.c decommit_pages) maps fresh
zero-fill pages over the range and leaves them readable and writable,
the contract LookupCache's VirtualDontNeed(..., false) of the L1 array
the JIT reads already relies on. The reset now makes the MEM_DECOMMIT
alone there: the pages are zeroed and returned as before, without the
query and the recommit. VirtualDontNeed also queries the protection only
when it recommits, which saves that query for LookupCache's clears.

Linear: PLA-610
Class: ios-port
Evidence: .work/hud-diag/s1-host.log ([callret], [inv-census], [dc-census]), .work/scratch/pla610/s3-exc/REPORT.md
Offered-upstream: no; the query-only-to-recommit half could be, the rest is the iOS decommit's
---
 FEXCore/Source/Interface/Core/Core.cpp         | 18 ++++++++++++++----
 .../FEXCore/Debug/InternalThreadState.h        |  8 ++++----
 FEXCore/include/FEXCore/Utils/AllocatorHooks.h | 10 ++++++----
 3 files changed, 24 insertions(+), 12 deletions(-)

diff --git a/FEXCore/Source/Interface/Core/Core.cpp b/FEXCore/Source/Interface/Core/Core.cpp
index a610b54..c6dded0 100644
--- a/FEXCore/Source/Interface/Core/Core.cpp
+++ b/FEXCore/Source/Interface/Core/Core.cpp
@@ -681,11 +681,10 @@ void ContextImpl::ClearCodeCache(FEXCore::Core::InternalThreadState* Thread, boo
  *     established; that is what the unix-side census below measures.)
  *
  *  2. THE CLEAR RECLAIMS -- IT DOES NOT DIRTY. VirtualDontNeed() here is
- *     VirtualFree(MEM_DECOMMIT) + VirtualAlloc(MEM_COMMIT). This stack is not
+ *     VirtualFree(MEM_DECOMMIT) alone on iOS (PLA-610). This stack is not
  *     pool-aliased, so wine's decommit_pages() (virtual_ios.c) takes the
- *     anon_mmap_fixed() branch: a fresh MAP_ANON|MAP_FIXED over the range, which
- *     DROPS the old physical pages and installs zero-fill-on-demand. The
- *     MEM_COMMIT that follows only restores access; it does not touch pages.
+ *     anon_mmap_fixed() branch: a fresh read/write MAP_ANON|MAP_FIXED over the
+ *     range, which DROPS the old physical pages and installs zero-fill-on-demand.
  *     So the full clear was RETURNING up to 16MB per reset, and ml609's 4MB
  *     version left the rest of each stack resident.
  *
@@ -746,7 +745,18 @@ void ResetCallRetStack(FEXCore::Core::InternalThreadState* Thread, const char* S
   uint64_t ResetT0, ResetT1, ResetFreq;
   __asm__ volatile("mrs %0, cntvct_el0" : "=r"(ResetT0));
 #endif
+#ifdef FEX_IOS_HOST
+  // Playport (PLA-610): one MEM_DECOMMIT, without the query and MEM_COMMIT around it.
+  // Wine's decommit on iOS (virtual_ios.c decommit_pages) maps fresh zero pages over
+  // the range and leaves it readable and writable, the contract LookupCache's
+  // VirtualDontNeed(..., false) of the L1 array the JIT reads already relies on; the
+  // pages are returned as before. A reset ran under the code invalidation mutex for
+  // every code invalidation that found blocks of the thread, and in World of
+  // Warcraft's SMC storms the three Wine calls took 60-180 us a reset.
+  FEXCore::Allocator::VirtualDontNeed(Thread->CallRetStackBase, TS::CALLRET_STACK_SIZE, false);
+#else
   FEXCore::Allocator::VirtualDontNeed(Thread->CallRetStackBase, TS::CALLRET_STACK_SIZE);
+#endif
 #if defined(ARCHITECTURE_arm64) || defined(ARCHITECTURE_arm64ec)
   __asm__ volatile("mrs %0, cntvct_el0" : "=r"(ResetT1));
   __asm__ volatile("mrs %0, cntfrq_el0" : "=r"(ResetFreq));
diff --git a/FEXCore/include/FEXCore/Debug/InternalThreadState.h b/FEXCore/include/FEXCore/Debug/InternalThreadState.h
index 036bcd6..ca2a579 100644
--- a/FEXCore/include/FEXCore/Debug/InternalThreadState.h
+++ b/FEXCore/include/FEXCore/Debug/InternalThreadState.h
@@ -136,11 +136,11 @@ struct alignas(FEXCore::Utils::FEX_PAGE_SIZE) InternalThreadState : public FEXCo
   //   (a) Dispatcher.cpp's JITCallback sentinel push tests the WHOLE stack, so
   //       the callback path is not bounded by this window at all.
   //
-  //   (b) The clear RECLAIMS rather than dirties. VirtualDontNeed() is
-  //       MEM_DECOMMIT + MEM_COMMIT, and on this (non-pool-aliased) range wine's
+  //   (b) The clear RECLAIMS rather than dirties. On iOS VirtualDontNeed() is a
+  //       MEM_DECOMMIT alone (PLA-610), and on this (non-pool-aliased) range wine's
   //       decommit_pages() does anon_mmap_fixed() — a fresh MAP_ANON|MAP_FIXED
-  //       that drops the physical pages and installs zero-fill-on-demand. The
-  //       recommit only restores access. So a full-size clear RETURNS memory,
+  //       read/write mapping that drops the physical pages and installs
+  //       zero-fill-on-demand. So a full-size clear RETURNS memory,
   //       and shrinking it strands the remainder resident.
   //
   // Clear CALLRET_STACK_SIZE. These constants describe the guard, not the cost.
diff --git a/FEXCore/include/FEXCore/Utils/AllocatorHooks.h b/FEXCore/include/FEXCore/Utils/AllocatorHooks.h
index 7a07a73..c7deede 100644
--- a/FEXCore/include/FEXCore/Utils/AllocatorHooks.h
+++ b/FEXCore/include/FEXCore/Utils/AllocatorHooks.h
@@ -157,13 +157,15 @@ inline void VirtualFree(void* Ptr, size_t Size) {
 }
 
 inline void VirtualDontNeed(void* Ptr, size_t Size, bool Recommit = true) {
-  // Zero the page-aligned region, preserving permissions.
+  // Zero the page-aligned region, preserving permissions: only a recommit needs them.
+  if (!Recommit) {
+    ::VirtualFree(Ptr, Size, MEM_DECOMMIT);
+    return;
+  }
   MEMORY_BASIC_INFORMATION Info;
   ::VirtualQuery(Ptr, &Info, sizeof(Info));
   ::VirtualFree(Ptr, Size, MEM_DECOMMIT);
-  if (Recommit) {
-    ::VirtualAlloc(Ptr, Size, MEM_COMMIT, Info.Protect);
-  }
+  ::VirtualAlloc(Ptr, Size, MEM_COMMIT, Info.Protect);
 }
 
 inline bool VirtualProtect(void* Ptr, size_t Size, ProtectOptions options) {
